ir nights off if you're already  missing out on regular sleep you might  as well fully commit right the cast got  by on cat naps and caught up on sleep  during the day when possible becoming a  Disney Channel star means giving up a  lot of your individual freedom Disney  Channel contracts are strict and they  require actors to commit completely  Disney Channel even controls what the  Stars can post on their social media we  don't just mean post about the movies  they're in that's an important part of  it they can't post spoilers or any  behind-the-scenes details Disney doesn't  want leaked but the rest of their posts  are monitored by Disney - they can't  represent brands that Disney doesn't  approve of they can't post aspects of  their life that are too serious and they  can't be too controversial everything  they post on any platform has to fit the  image of a perfect Disney Channel star  even if it's not entirely true Disney  Channel even controls what its stars  wear in public they can't wear anything  deemed too appropriate or revealing even  on their own time this is the case for  every star including the cast of zombies  - you're beautiful at ease  zombies and zombies too are somewhat  different from other Disney Channel  original movies the cast of each movie  was allowed a degree of creative freedom  they wanted the characters to feel  authentic in zombies the zombies were  able to spice up the costumes they added  elements that they liked and wanted but  it had to fit a few guidelines first of  all it had to make sense for the  character it also had to fit with the  general vibe of the zombies costumes and  makeup zombie football star presidential  hopeful the werewolf's had the same  freedom with some restrictions anything  they added needed to fit a certain color  scheme and style but they could add  things to their costume the cast was  also allowed to add their own spin to  their dance moves as long as they  followed the general choreography they  could move their arms or legs in ways  that felt natural again  this had to fit their individual  character this creative freedom made all  the characters come alive and feel  original it was important because the  message of the franchise is that being  an individual matters Disney Channel  wants its cast members to be close  friends it helps boost their image of a  positive friendly company for kids and  teens so cast bonding is never  discouraged the zombies to cast took  this very seriously  a lot of their bonding moments were  self-imposed in the first movie they  hosted a bunch of dance parties they  continued that tradition on zombies too  they also hosted a bunch of game nights  after rehearsals or during time off  while filming they would play all sorts  of board games together they also had  pool parties the returning cast wasn't  about to exclude the werewolf's either  they were invited to hang out with  everyone on the very first day we'd love  that they are all such great friends it  also made the movie so much better  because they all had great chemistry  which rule would be the hardest for you  to follow let us know in the comments  that's a wrap give this video a thumbs  up and click that subscribe button  thanks for watching we'll see you next  time on the things  [Music]
 

